[h1]R.A.T.S. Flotilla[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

[b]Is it the game or a mod? Check it on a clean copy.[/b]
A test bench for Sea Power: several installs side by side, each with its own mods, settings and saves.

[quote]▶ [b]A small Windows app, not a game mod:[/b] leave it off in the game's Mods menu
▶ [b]Step by step:[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3836683383]the Flotilla guide[/url]
✉ Bugs, ideas, questions: [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/flotilla]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]
⭐ A favourite helps other captains find it[/quote]

[h2]✦ New in 0.3[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Mods follow the game:[/b] after an Update, every mod in that copy is checked the way the game checks it
[*][b]Refresh from Workshop[/b] for mods you keep in one copy
[/list]

[h2]✦ Highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Bug reports that hold up.[/b] Reproduce it on a clean install with no mods and no loader
[*][b]Test mod sets[/b] on a copy loaded to the gills; your everyday game stays as it is
[*][b]Keep an old version[/b] next to the new one after a game update, and compare
[*][b]For modders:[/b] try a build on its own copy, against the game version you pick
[*][b]Your Steam install is never changed[/b]
[/list]

[h2]▶ Quick start[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe and let Steam download it
[*]Open [i]steamapps\workshop\content\1286220\3836624723[/i] in the Steam library that holds Sea Power
[*]Start [b]SeaPowerFlotilla.exe[/b] once: it moves to a safe place and offers a desktop shortcut
[/olist]
[list]
[*][b]Windows says "unknown publisher"?[/b] More info, Run anyway; no admin rights needed
[*][b]Needs .NET Framework 4.8[/b] (every Windows 10 and 11 has it)
[*][b]Plain download:[/b] [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerFlotilla/releases]GitHub[/url]
[/list]

[h2]⚙ What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]New copy:[/b] Clean (game files only, fresh settings) or your whole setup; about 19 GB each
[*][b]Play:[/b] the copy you pick, with its own settings, load order and saves
[*][b]Mods:[/b] on/off and order per copy, a mod from a folder or .zip for one copy, the game version each was made for
[*][b]Keep in this copy:[/b] freeze a Workshop mod there; Refresh from Workshop or Use Workshop again when you want
[*][b]Update:[/b] refresh a copy's game files, keep its mods and saves; or keep the older version
[*][b]Rename, desktop shortcut, Delete[/b]
[/list]

[h2]⚠ Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Subscriptions are your Steam account's:[/b] every copy sees them; which are on, and the order, is per copy
[*][b]Mods with scripts[/b] need a mod loader in that copy: Keel or Anchor Chain, either one; a Clean copy has none, on purpose
[*][b]One Sea Power at a time;[/b] don't start the game from Steam while a copy runs
[*][b]The data folder[/b] is switched to the copy's while it runs and put back when the game closes
[*][b]Copies are not synced[/b] to Steam Cloud, and Steam updates only its own install
[/list]

